target loom, resume
 1 record: record a new revision of loom (revision 20260922-120000; commit 0123456789ab; signed by kyle@example.com (SHA256:AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz0123456789abcdefg))
 2 edge: run the edge, the app's own network and the one it shares with the edge alone
 3 dns: confirm core.example.com, runner.example.com point at this machine
 4 inherit: copy parent's secrets to loom, which runs its code
 5 secrets: make the secrets the manifest asks for: the database's password, the object store's root user, 2 generated, 3 derived
 6 data: keep the app's data: postgres 17, object store, volume core-data (restore database from /restore/pg.dump; files from /restore/files.tar.gz)
 7 build-core-api: build core-api's image from ., for core-api, product, schema (target server)
 8 pull-objects-setup: use image quay.io/minio/mc:latest for objects-setup
 9 build-runner: build runner from . (target runner-runtime)
10 release-checkpoint: capture and retain a quiesced checkpoint before a data release with compatibility unknown data release
11 release: run objects-setup, schema, once each, before anything new starts
12 start: start 3 container(s) (revision 20260922-120000; secrets: DATABASE_URL, LOOM_CORE_API_DATABASE_URL)
13 ready: wait until every workload answers
14 switch: route the edge to the new revision
15 certificates: wait for certificates for core.example.com, runner.example.com
16 retire: stop the revision this one replaces
